# A CANDIDATE: A CLIP'S LAST WORD IS KEPT (the speech port's fade-out;
# docs/notes/omnivoice-on-our-backend.md §15). engine-park.series, the LIVE
# engine ed93e3c1b2e2, line for line, then:
#   0030  the fade-out lasts as long as the trailing silence the trim kept
#         (at most 100 ms, never under 5 ms), where it faded the last 100 ms
#         whatever they held: a clip ending at its word kept the word faded
#         away (30 of 40 clips read aloud faded speech). A clip with 100 ms
#         of its own silence is the same bytes as before. And the joined
#         audio before any trim or fade, dumped with MTMD_DEBUG_OMNIVOICE.
#   SERIES_FILE=deploy/localai/patches/staged/engine-fade.series \
#     sh deploy/localai/llama-cpp/build.sh sycl_f16 <out dir>      # the live INTEL_STACK
# ANOTHER ENGINE: a build and every gate again. Only the speech port's
# post-processing changes, and only a clip's last 100 ms; no other model's
# answer can move (the patch touches tools/mtmd's speech pipeline alone).
base dd5780aa904d132c784867d37fc713df8d984c8a
